ent. Raters are slightly more cautious at Lean D and no surveys have been published since mid-August, so the forecast sits near six points with wide uncertainty.", "watch": "Fresh polling after mid-August — particularly if the 'predator protector' attacks or a split among Mormon women move swing voters — could tighten the race and pull this toward Lean D.", "confidence": "medium", "notes": ["Incumbent Katie Hobbs (D) is running."]}, "overview": "Arizona's governor's race pits incumbent Democrat Katie Hobbs against Republican Andy Biggs, a former Freedom Caucus chairman, in a state that leans slightly Republican overall. Polling since late July has consistently shown Hobbs ahead, with margins ranging from four to fifteen points and an average near eight. She has also raised about $10 million to Biggs' $3 million, giving her a clear financial edge, and prediction markets put her chances near 88 percent.\n\nBiggs' polarizing profile is the central question: surveys show independents and women moving toward Hobbs, though a Republican-sponsored August poll showed the race at just one point. Most rating outlets call the race Lean Democratic, with one at Likely Democratic. The last public polls date to mid-August, so late-breaking attacks and a shifting electorate could still tighten the contest in a state with a history of narrow margins.", "history": [{"date": "2026-09-22", "p_dem": 0.9144, "margin": 7.07}, {"date": "2026-09-23", "p_dem": 0.9047, "margin": 7.0}, {"date": "2026-09-24", "p_dem": 0.9201, "margin": 7.5}, {"date": "2026-09-25", "p_dem": 0.9198, "margin": 7.5}, {"date": "2026-09-26", "p_dem": 0.8839, "margin": 7.0}, {"date": "2026-09-27", "p_dem": 0.8882, "margin": 7.0}, {"date": "2026-09-28", "p_dem": 0.8963, "margin": 7.0}, {"date": "2026-09-29", "p_dem": 0.8934, "margin": 6.5}, {"date": "2026-09-30", "p_dem": 0.8924, "margin": 6.8}, {"date": "2026-10-01", "p_dem": 0.8871, "margin": 6.5}, {"date": "2026-10-02", "p_dem": 0.8786, "margin": 6.5}]}